{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZvvxZ5LDaHv44kL8ni6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a complete picture. Let me summarize my findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt:11` - no status field\n- OrderRepository: `OrderRepository.kt` - in-memory store with save/findById/existsById/findAll\n- OrderController: `OrderController.kt` - has POST /orders, GET /orders/{orderId}, GET /orders\n- Shipment entity: `Shipment.kt:9` - has status field (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentRepository: `ShipmentRepository.kt` - no method to find shipments by orderId\n- ShipmentController: `ShipmentController.kt` - has POST /shipments, GET /shipments/{shipmentId}, GET /shipments\n- API error handling: `ApiExceptions.kt` - ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409)\n- ErrorCode enum: `ApiError.kt:31` - ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n\n**Conventions:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses\n- GlobalExceptionHandler converts them to ApiError envelopes with status codes\n- Tests assert both status and error body structure\n- Error envelope: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [] } }`\n- Test patterns use MockMvc with helper functions for common operations\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. Order.kt - add status field\n2. OrderRepository.kt - add method to find shipments by orderId (or add to ShipmentRepository)\n3. OrderController.kt - add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint\n4. ShipmentRepository.kt - add findByOrderId method\n5. ShipmentController.kt - prevent creating shipments for CANCELLED orders\n6. ApiError.kt - add error codes for cancelled order scenarios\n7. OrderControllerTest.kt - add tests for cancel endpoint\n\n**Risks:**\n- Race conditions: need atomic check-and-update for shipments\n- Idempotency: cancelling already-cancelled order must succeed\n- All-or-nothing: if any shipment is CONFIRMED, nothing should change\n\n**Open questions:** None - ticket is clear on all requirements.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add an `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and a `status` field to the Order data class. New orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** - Add a `findByOrderId` method to ShipmentRepository to query shipments by order ID (needed to implement cancel logic).\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method.\n\n4. **ApiError.kt** - Add new error codes: `ORDER_CANCELLED` (for creating shipments on cancelled orders), and potentially `ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL` (for CONFIRMED shipments blocking cancel).\n\n5. **OrderController.kt** - Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Returns 404 if order doesn't exist\n   - Returns 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED (with no changes)\n   - Cancels all CREATED shipments and transitions order to CANCELLED\n   - Returns the cancelled order\n   - Idempotent: if already CANCELLED, succeeds with no change\n\n6. **ShipmentController.kt** - In the create method, check if order is CANCELLED and reject with 409 if so.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add comprehensive tests for the cancel endpoint covering all scenarios.\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Considered adding an OrderService layer for business logic, but the existing codebase uses controllers directly with the repository, so I'll stay consistent with that pattern.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel active order with CREATED shipments:**\n   - Read order (404 if missing)\n   - Read all shipments for order\n   - Check no shipment is CONFIRMED (409 if found)\n   - Update order to CANCELLED\n   - Update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n   - Return order\n\n2. **Cancel already-cancelled order:**\n   - Read order (404 if missing)\n   - Order already CANCELLED → success, no change\n\n3. **Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment:**\n   - Read order (404 if missing)\n   - Read all shipments\n   - Find CONFIRMED shipment → throw 409 ConflictException\n   - No database changes\n\n4. **Create shipment for cancelled order:**\n   - Check order exists (existing behavior)\n   - Check order is not CANCELLED → throw 409 if so\n   - Create shipment\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test cancel active order with CREATED shipments → order and shipments updated\n- Test cancel already-cancelled order → succeeds, no change\n- Test cancel with CONFIRMED shipment → 409, nothing changes\n- Test cancel non-existent order → 404\n- Test create shipment on cancelled order → 409\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":243,"cache_read_input_tokens":22660,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":243},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2638fac-a5b0-434b-a34e-40015c9eee32","uuid":"d9055af9-d310-47f4-b891-0428c3ce0a93","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:21:53.515Z","request_id":"req_011CfZvvx7YPAj7rAs8S9z6R"}
