{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZw6B1BGaN82L3v3FHGu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! All 21 tests pass. Let me review the changes I made:\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — `./mvnw test` returns BUILD SUCCESS with 21 tests passing\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All 4 original OrderControllerTest, 5 original ShipmentControllerTest, and other tests still pass\n3. ✅ **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel cancels active order, persists it, and cancels CREATED shipments** — OrderController.cancel() method handles this, tests: `cancels an active order and returns it with CANCELLED status`, `cancelling an active order with CREATED shipments cancels the shipments`\n4. ✅ **Error responses consistent with API** — Uses ConflictException (409), ResourceNotFoundException (404) with proper error codes through GlobalExceptionHandler\n5. ✅ **Retry idempotency, CONFIRMED blocking, unknown order, shipment for cancelled order** — Tests cover all these:\n   - `cancelling an already cancelled order succeeds and changes nothing`\n   - `cancel is rejected with 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED`\n   - `cancel on non-existent order returns 404`\n   - `rejects shipment creation for cancelled order with 409`\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency** — Only modified Kotlin/Spring code\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only changed order and shipment features plus API error codes\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Added OrderStatus enum and status field with default ACTIVE\n2. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added findByOrderId method to find shipments by order ID\n3. **ApiError.kt** — Added ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL and ORDER_CANCELLED error codes\n4. **OrderController.kt** — Added cancel endpoint with proper error handling and idempotency\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added order dependency injection and validation to preven